albums with The Clash, which in turn was a copy of Elvis Presley's debut album.","title":"F-Punk"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"My Chemical Romance (often abbreviated as MCR) was an American rock band from Newark, New Jersey, active from 2001 to 2013.","title":"My Chemical Romance"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The band's best-known lineup consisted of lead vocalist Gerard Way, guitarists Ray Toro and Frank Iero, bassist Mikey Way and drummer Bob Bryar.","title":"My Chemical Romance"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Founded by Gerard, Mikey, Toro, Matt Pelissier, and later joined by Iero, the band signed to Eyeball Records and released their debut album "I Brought You My Bullets, You Brought Me Your Love" in 2002.","title":"My Chemical Romance"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" They signed with Reprise Records the next year and released their major label debut "Three Cheers for Sweet Revenge" in 2004.","title":"My Chemical Romance"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Shortly after the album's release, Pelissier was replaced by Bob Bryar.","title":"My Chemical Romance"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" A commercial success, the album was awarded platinum status over a year later.","title":"My Chemical Romance"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mick Jones is singer-songwriter Mick Jones' self-titled debut/studio album, released in 1989.","title":"Mick Jones (album)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Jones is one of the original members of the group Foreigner.","title":"Mick Jones (album)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The album was Mick Jones' only solo release.","title":"Mick Jones (album)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gary Stonadge is a British bass guitarist and DJ.","title":"Gary Stonadge"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He started playing in Mick Jones' band Big Audio Dynamite in 1989 when he changed the previous lineup completely and renamed it Big Audio Dynamite II.","title":"Gary Stonadge"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He left in 1995 after recording 5 albums with them.","title":"Gary Stonadge"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Since then he concentrated on DJ sets, playing at clubs and bars mainly in New York and London.","title":"Gary Stonadge"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He is currently playing with Mick Jones in The Rotten Hill Gang.","title":"Gary Stonadge"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: musician
